1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:04,448
Percent questions look easy, and
that's exactly why they cost points.

2
00:00:04,468 --> 00:00:09,020
The SAT writes them so that the
obvious move gives you a wrong answer,

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:12,467
and that wrong answer is sitting
right there in the choices.

4
00:00:12,543 --> 00:00:16,971
The big three mistakes: adding percent
changes that should be multiplied,

5
00:00:17,257 --> 00:00:20,292
dividing by the wrong
number in a percent change,

6
00:00:20,364 --> 00:00:23,543
and undoing a discount by
adding the percent back on.

7
00:00:23,587 --> 00:00:28,444
In this video, you'll learn one tool that
handles almost every percent question:

8
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,623
the multiplier.

9
00:00:29,659 --> 00:00:33,281
Then we'll use it on every
question type the SAT likes,

10
00:00:33,301 --> 00:00:36,479
with seven practice questions
that get harder as we go.

11
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,873
Start with the basics.

12
00:00:37,893 --> 00:00:42,643
Percent means per hundred, so twenty
percent is twenty over one hundred,

13
00:00:42,714 --> 00:00:44,785
or zero point two.

14
00:00:44,892 --> 00:00:48,123
Twenty percent of fifty is
zero point two times fifty,

15
00:00:48,143 --> 00:00:49,320
which is ten.

16
00:00:49,785 --> 00:00:52,497
In percent questions, the
word of means multiply.

17
00:00:52,517 --> 00:00:54,017
Now the key idea.

18
00:00:54,124 --> 00:00:57,445
A percent increase or
decrease is just a multiplier.

19
00:00:57,517 --> 00:01:01,282
Increase by twenty percent, and you
keep the whole thing plus twenty percent

20
00:01:01,302 --> 00:01:01,853
more.

21
00:01:01,873 --> 00:01:06,409
That's one plus zero point
two, or times one point two.

22
00:01:06,448 --> 00:01:09,748
Decrease by fifteen percent, and
you keep eighty-five percent,

23
00:01:09,768 --> 00:01:12,642
so multiply by zero point eight five.

24
00:01:12,662 --> 00:01:16,642
An increase of six percent
is times one point zero six.

25
00:01:16,662 --> 00:01:20,126
A decrease of forty percent
is times zero point six.

26
00:01:20,181 --> 00:01:23,553
Once you think in
multipliers, the rest follows.

27
00:01:23,573 --> 00:01:24,697
Changes in a row?

28
00:01:24,717 --> 00:01:26,411
Multiply the multipliers.

29
00:01:26,431 --> 00:01:27,874
Need the original value?

30
00:01:27,894 --> 00:01:29,231
Divide by the multiplier.

31
00:01:29,251 --> 00:01:31,738
That's most of this
video in two sentences.

32
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:35,237
Percentages are one of the skills in
Problem-Solving and Data Analysis,

33
00:01:35,257 --> 00:01:38,650
which is about fifteen
percent of the math section.

34
00:01:38,686 --> 00:01:42,011
The questions come in a
handful of predictable types.

35
00:01:42,031 --> 00:01:44,709
What percent one number is of another.

36
00:01:44,888 --> 00:01:47,817
Percent change from an
old value to a new one.

37
00:01:47,853 --> 00:01:49,423
Two changes in a row.

38
00:01:49,496 --> 00:01:52,031
Working backward to an original value.

39
00:01:52,103 --> 00:01:54,067
A percent of a percent.

40
00:01:54,281 --> 00:01:56,190
And percentage points versus percent.

41
00:01:56,210 --> 00:01:57,388
We'll go in that order.

42
00:01:57,424 --> 00:01:58,511
Question one.

43
00:01:58,531 --> 00:02:02,353
In a class of thirty-two students,
twelve play an instrument.

44
00:02:02,496 --> 00:02:05,934
What percent of the students in
the class play an instrument?

45
00:02:05,954 --> 00:02:07,133
Pause and try it.

46
00:02:10,329 --> 00:02:12,666
What percent questions
are part over whole,

47
00:02:12,686 --> 00:02:14,042
times one hundred.

48
00:02:14,079 --> 00:02:16,666
The part is twelve, and
the whole is thirty-two.

49
00:02:16,686 --> 00:02:21,630
Twelve divided by thirty-two
is zero point three seven five.

50
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:24,945
Times one hundred, that's
thirty-seven point five percent.

51
00:02:24,965 --> 00:02:27,214
Type thirty-seven point five.

52
00:02:27,928 --> 00:02:31,929
The test directions say not to
include symbols like a percent sign.

53
00:02:32,071 --> 00:02:34,428
And always ask, part of what?

54
00:02:35,322 --> 00:02:38,179
Here, the whole is the entire class.

55
00:02:38,243 --> 00:02:39,223
Question two.

56
00:02:39,243 --> 00:02:42,759
The price of a concert ticket increased
from sixty-four dollars to eighty

57
00:02:42,779 --> 00:02:43,759
dollars.

58
00:02:43,779 --> 00:02:45,921
By what percent did the price increase?

59
00:02:45,947 --> 00:02:47,126
Pause and try it.

60
00:02:50,322 --> 00:02:54,016
Percent change is the change,
divided by the original,

61
00:02:54,036 --> 00:02:55,465
times one hundred.

62
00:02:55,572 --> 00:02:57,980
The change is eighty minus sixty-four,

63
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,266
which is sixteen.

64
00:02:59,286 --> 00:03:01,036
The original is sixty-four.

65
00:03:01,107 --> 00:03:03,623
Sixteen over sixty-four is one fourth,

66
00:03:03,643 --> 00:03:05,302
which is twenty-five percent.

67
00:03:05,322 --> 00:03:06,858
The answer is C.

68
00:03:06,903 --> 00:03:08,989
The trap is B, twenty percent.

69
00:03:09,009 --> 00:03:11,954
That's sixteen divided
by eighty, the new price.

70
00:03:11,974 --> 00:03:13,989
Always divide by the starting value.

71
00:03:14,009 --> 00:03:16,633
A is the change in dollars, not a percent.

72
00:03:16,653 --> 00:03:21,260
And eighty percent is the old
price as a percent of the new one.

73
00:03:22,117 --> 00:03:26,889
Multiplier check: sixty-four times
one point two five is eighty.

74
00:03:26,909 --> 00:03:27,889
Question three.

75
00:03:27,909 --> 00:03:31,266
A store increased the price
of a jacket by forty percent.

76
00:03:31,302 --> 00:03:35,623
During a sale, the store then decreased
the new price by twenty-five percent.

77
00:03:35,837 --> 00:03:39,051
The sale price is what
percent of the original price?

78
00:03:39,075 --> 00:03:40,253
Pause and try it.

79
00:03:43,449 --> 00:03:45,928
Two changes in a row
means two multipliers.

80
00:03:45,948 --> 00:03:49,394
A forty percent increase
is times one point four.

81
00:03:49,414 --> 00:03:53,464
A twenty-five percent decrease
is times zero point seven five.

82
00:03:53,484 --> 00:03:54,770
Multiply them.

83
00:03:55,056 --> 00:03:58,771
One point four times zero point
seven five is one point zero five.

84
00:03:58,826 --> 00:04:01,733
So the sale price is one point
zero five times the original.

85
00:04:01,753 --> 00:04:03,341
That's one hundred five percent of it.

86
00:04:03,361 --> 00:04:04,754
The answer is B.

87
00:04:04,801 --> 00:04:05,531
The trap is C.

88
00:04:05,551 --> 00:04:10,015
Forty minus twenty-five is fifteen,
but percent changes don't add.

89
00:04:10,158 --> 00:04:12,602
The sale takes twenty-five
percent of the higher,

90
00:04:12,622 --> 00:04:14,801
marked-up price, not of the original.

91
00:04:14,836 --> 00:04:16,657
D ignores the sale.

92
00:04:17,015 --> 00:04:20,801
And A comes from subtracting the
multipliers instead of multiplying them.

93
00:04:20,857 --> 00:04:21,944
Question four.

94
00:04:21,964 --> 00:04:26,159
After a fifteen percent discount, a
pair of headphones costs one hundred two

95
00:04:26,179 --> 00:04:26,944
dollars.

96
00:04:26,964 --> 00:04:29,687
What was the price of the
headphones before the discount?

97
00:04:29,707 --> 00:04:30,886
Pause and try it.

98
00:04:34,082 --> 00:04:36,168
Write it as a multiplier equation.

99
00:04:36,188 --> 00:04:40,205
A fifteen percent discount is
times zero point eight five.

100
00:04:40,225 --> 00:04:43,061
So the original price,
times zero point eight five,

101
00:04:43,081 --> 00:04:44,939
equals one hundred two.

102
00:04:44,996 --> 00:04:47,139
To undo a multiplier, divide by it.

103
00:04:47,175 --> 00:04:51,476
One hundred two divided by zero point
eight five is one hundred twenty.

104
00:04:51,496 --> 00:04:52,941
The answer is D.

105
00:04:52,961 --> 00:04:53,834
Check it.

106
00:04:53,854 --> 00:04:57,191
Fifteen percent of one
hundred twenty is eighteen,

107
00:04:57,211 --> 00:05:00,568
and one hundred twenty minus
eighteen is one hundred two.

108
00:05:00,589 --> 00:05:05,104
C is the classic trap: adding fifteen
percent back onto one hundred two.

109
00:05:05,124 --> 00:05:08,446
That gives one hundred seventeen
dollars and thirty cents.

110
00:05:08,589 --> 00:05:12,389
But the discount was fifteen
percent of the original price,

111
00:05:12,409 --> 00:05:14,246
not of one hundred two.

112
00:05:14,266 --> 00:05:17,874
B adds fifteen dollars
instead of fifteen percent.

113
00:05:17,946 --> 00:05:20,696
And A takes the discount a second time.

114
00:05:20,731 --> 00:05:21,890
Question five.

115
00:05:21,910 --> 00:05:27,624
The number a is thirty percent of b,
and b is one hundred fifty percent of c.

116
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:30,248
The number a is what percent of c?

117
00:05:30,268 --> 00:05:31,446
Pause and try it.

118
00:05:35,642 --> 00:05:36,979
Translate each sentence.

119
00:05:36,999 --> 00:05:40,122
Is means equals, and of means multiply.

120
00:05:40,142 --> 00:05:44,729
a is thirty percent of b means
a equals zero point three b.

121
00:05:44,749 --> 00:05:49,606
b is one hundred fifty percent of
c means b equals one point five c.

122
00:05:49,633 --> 00:05:50,755
Substitute.

123
00:05:50,775 --> 00:05:54,113
a equals zero point three
times one point five c,

124
00:05:54,133 --> 00:05:56,291
which is zero point four five c.

125
00:05:56,311 --> 00:05:59,363
So a is forty-five percent of c.

126
00:05:59,383 --> 00:06:00,990
The answer is forty-five.

127
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:04,547
If the letters feel abstract,
pick c equals one hundred.

128
00:06:04,567 --> 00:06:08,619
Then b is one hundred fifty,
and a is thirty percent of that,

129
00:06:08,639 --> 00:06:09,440
which is forty-five.

130
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:13,727
Forty-five out of one hundred
is forty-five percent.

131
00:06:13,747 --> 00:06:18,620
Starting with one hundred works on almost
any percent question that gives you no

132
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,747
real numbers.

133
00:06:19,823 --> 00:06:22,716
Next, a trap that shows
up in data questions.

134
00:06:22,751 --> 00:06:26,660
When a percentage changes, there
are two ways to describe the change.

135
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:29,231
Percentage points are
a simple subtraction.

136
00:06:29,251 --> 00:06:32,892
Percent change compares that
difference to the starting percentage.

137
00:06:32,911 --> 00:06:33,963
Question six.

138
00:06:33,983 --> 00:06:38,284
In a town, eight percent of residents
biked to work in twenty eighteen,

139
00:06:38,304 --> 00:06:41,733
and ten percent of residents biked
to work in twenty twenty-four.

140
00:06:41,982 --> 00:06:45,499
The twenty twenty-four percentage is
what percent greater than the twenty

141
00:06:45,519 --> 00:06:46,839
eighteen percentage?

142
00:06:46,861 --> 00:06:48,039
Pause and try it.

143
00:06:52,235 --> 00:06:55,699
Ten percent minus eight percent
is two percentage points.

144
00:06:56,128 --> 00:06:58,251
But the question asks
what percent greater.

145
00:06:58,271 --> 00:07:00,287
That's percent change: the difference,

146
00:07:00,307 --> 00:07:03,449
two, divided by the starting value, eight.

147
00:07:03,592 --> 00:07:06,628
Two over eight is one fourth,
or twenty-five percent.

148
00:07:06,699 --> 00:07:08,092
The answer is C.

149
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:13,279
A, two percent, is the percentage
point difference written as a percent.

150
00:07:13,422 --> 00:07:14,672
That's the trap.

151
00:07:14,779 --> 00:07:17,329
B divides by the newer value.

152
00:07:17,349 --> 00:07:19,865
And D, one hundred twenty-five percent,

153
00:07:19,885 --> 00:07:24,061
is what percent ten is of eight,
not how much greater it is.

154
00:07:24,081 --> 00:07:25,954
Question seven, the hardest one.

155
00:07:25,974 --> 00:07:29,760
A bookstore increased the price
of a book by twenty percent.

156
00:07:29,831 --> 00:07:33,759
A month later, it decreased the
new price by twenty percent.

157
00:07:33,867 --> 00:07:38,240
After both changes, the book cost
thirty-three dollars and sixty cents.

158
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:40,347
What was the price of
the book, in dollars,

159
00:07:40,367 --> 00:07:42,007
before both changes?

160
00:07:42,027 --> 00:07:42,686
Pause and try it.

161
00:07:42,706 --> 00:07:44,383
Take a little longer on this one.

162
00:07:48,609 --> 00:07:50,501
First, the trap.

163
00:07:50,573 --> 00:07:53,946
Up twenty percent and then down
twenty percent feels like it cancels,

164
00:07:53,966 --> 00:07:55,981
so you'd answer thirty-three sixty.

165
00:07:56,001 --> 00:07:57,410
It doesn't cancel.

166
00:07:57,430 --> 00:08:00,231
The multipliers are one point
two and zero point eight,

167
00:08:00,251 --> 00:08:03,644
and one point two times zero point
eight is zero point nine six.

168
00:08:03,743 --> 00:08:06,757
So the original price,
times zero point nine six,

169
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:08,794
equals thirty-three sixty.

170
00:08:08,814 --> 00:08:09,850
Divide.

171
00:08:09,957 --> 00:08:13,757
Thirty-three point six divided by
zero point nine six is thirty-five.

172
00:08:13,777 --> 00:08:16,635
The original price was
thirty-five dollars.

173
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,557
Check it forward.

174
00:08:17,577 --> 00:08:20,077
Thirty-five, up twenty
percent, is forty-two.

175
00:08:20,112 --> 00:08:23,200
Forty-two, down twenty
percent, is thirty-three sixty.

176
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:24,246
It works.

177
00:08:24,266 --> 00:08:26,802
Desmos shortcut, if you'd
rather skip the algebra.

178
00:08:27,052 --> 00:08:31,981
Graph y equals x times one point
two times zero point eight.

179
00:08:32,124 --> 00:08:35,159
Then graph y equals
thirty-three point six.

180
00:08:35,302 --> 00:08:37,031
Zoom out and click the intersection.

181
00:08:37,051 --> 00:08:39,928
It's at thirty-five,
thirty-three point six.

182
00:08:39,948 --> 00:08:43,090
Here's the test-day method
for every percent question.

183
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:47,483
Step one: turn every percent
change into a multiplier.

184
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:51,091
Up some percent means one plus
that percent as a decimal.

185
00:08:51,198 --> 00:08:53,052
Down means one minus it.

186
00:08:53,072 --> 00:08:55,643
Step two: decide the direction.

187
00:08:55,857 --> 00:08:57,730
Going forward from the original?

188
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:58,730
Multiply.

189
00:08:58,750 --> 00:09:00,659
Going backward to the original?

190
00:09:00,679 --> 00:09:01,623
Divide.

191
00:09:01,643 --> 00:09:03,158
More than one change?

192
00:09:03,178 --> 00:09:05,892
Multiply all the
multipliers together first.

193
00:09:05,948 --> 00:09:09,570
Step three: for percent
change and percent greater,

194
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:11,483
divide by the starting value.

195
00:09:11,626 --> 00:09:13,962
And if a question gives
you no real numbers,

196
00:09:13,982 --> 00:09:15,411
start with one hundred.

197
00:09:15,470 --> 00:09:16,450
Recap.

198
00:09:16,470 --> 00:09:18,307
Of means multiply.

199
00:09:18,327 --> 00:09:21,272
Percent change is the
change over the original.

200
00:09:21,292 --> 00:09:24,327
Changes in a row multiply, they don't add.

201
00:09:24,435 --> 00:09:27,199
To find the original,
divide by the multiplier.

202
00:09:27,219 --> 00:09:30,415
A percent of a percent
means multiply the decimals.

203
00:09:30,435 --> 00:09:33,185
And percentage points
aren't the same as percent.

204
00:09:33,231 --> 00:09:38,282
Every question here was written for this
video in the style of the real test.

205
00:09:38,302 --> 00:09:42,496
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

206
00:09:42,516 --> 00:09:44,588
skill, including percentages.

207
00:09:44,637 --> 00:09:46,331
If this helped, subscribe.

208
00:09:46,351 --> 00:09:49,494
The next video is SAT circles.
